# Project npm config for the system/ npm workspace. Every install of it runs
# here (CI, install_dependencies.sh, update-self, `cd system && npm ci`), so
# npm reads this file on all of them.
#
# onnxruntime-node (pulled in by @huggingface/transformers in
# libs/workspace_voice) ships its CPU binaries inside the npm package, but its
# postinstall script downloads the Linux x64 CUDA execution provider from the
# onnxruntime GitHub releases. Nothing here runs on a GPU, and that download
# failing (as it did when the release URL started answering 404) fails the
# whole install. `skip` is the value its install script documents for turning
# the download off; npm hands this key to the script as
# npm_config_onnxruntime_node_install_cuda. npm 11 warns that it does not know
# the key, and still passes it through.
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
